            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for a jacket, then the Urdu for pyjamas."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: چپل",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "چپل — chappal — \"a sandal, a slipper\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The origin of چپل (chappal) is uncertain, and CDIAL has no entry for it. DEDR, under Dravidian words for \"sandal\" such as Telugu ceppu, adds \"Cf. H. cappal\" (DEDR 1963): a comparison, not a settled source."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
